WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:04.467
There is a lot of unnecessary 
variation of treatment decisions,

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.000
especially in the Western world.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.049
You need to get in the front seat

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:11.049
with your doctor and start
sharing decisions on where to go.

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:14.467
Four questions, simple questions.

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:19.017
Consider them your new toolbox to help us.

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:21.586
Is this really necessary?

00:00:21.586 --> 00:00:23.440
What are the risks?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.941
Are there other options?

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:28.012
And what happens if I don't do anything?

00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:33.074
Ask them when your doctor
wants to send you to an MRI,

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:37.162
when he prescribes antibiotics,
or suggests an operation.

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:41.583
What we know from research
is that one out of five of you,

00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:45.128
20 percent, will change your
 opinion on what to do.

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:49.799
And by doing that, you will 
not only have made your life

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:53.094
a whole lot easier
and probably even better.

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:55.972
But the whole healthcare sector

00:00:55.972 --> 00:00:58.975
will have benefited from your decision.

